				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Crush cobble into gravel, sand, dust"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2101000000000203"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "exdeorum:wooden_hammer"
					tag: {
						Damage: 0
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&aHammer Time"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000015"]
			description: [
				"Craft an &eOak Sieve&r and a &eString Mesh&r, drop the mesh into the sieve, and sift your gravel, sand and dust."
				""
				"This is your mining replacement. Right-click to sift; &7hold right-click&r to keep going."
				""
				"&e&lHow sieving actually works.&r The block you put in decides &lwhat&r you can get. The mesh decides &lhow much of it&r and &lhow rare&r:"
				"&7- &fGravel&7 - metal ore chunks. Iron, copper, gold, tin, lead, aluminium."
				"&7- &fSand&7 - certus quartz, gunpowder, cocoa, sugar cane."
				"&7- &fDust&7 - redstone, lapis, glowstone, the rare stuff."
				"&7- &fCrushed netherrack / end stone&7 - nether and end drops without the trip."
				""
				"&e&lMesh tiers&r run &7string &8→ &7flint &8→ &7iron &8→ &7diamond &8→ &7netherite&r. Each tier does not just add new drops - it also &lraises the odds&r of everything below it. A diamond mesh on gravel pays far better than a string mesh on the same gravel."
				""
				"&8Do not throw meshes away when you upgrade. Multiple sieves running different meshes side by side is faster than one sieve you keep re-fitting."
				""
				"&7Sieving by hand is the early bottleneck. Look ahead to &fPowered Sieving&7 - the moment you automate this, the whole pack opens up.&r"
			]
			icon: "exdeorum:string_mesh"
			id: "2101000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				count: 16
				id: "2101000000000105"
				item: "minecraft:gravel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Your mining replacement"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "2101000000000204"
					item: "exdeorum:oak_sieve"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "2101000000000205"
					item: "exdeorum:string_mesh"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&aThe Sieve & the Mesh"
			x: -12.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000003"]
			description: [
				"Sift gravel and the void starts paying out. Ore chunks tumble free - iron, copper, gold, tin, lead and more."
				""
				"Collect your first chunks. Smelt them for ingots, or hold them for the machines that will multiply them later."
				""
				"&e&lDo not smelt everything.&r A chunk in a furnace is &l1 ingot&r. The same chunk, later, is worth far more:"
				"&7- &fMekanism Enrichment Chamber&7 - &a2x&7"
				"&7- &f+ Purification Chamber&7 - &a3x&7"
				"&7- &f+ Chemical Injection&7 - &a4x&7"
				"&7- &f+ Dissolution / full 5-stage&7 - &a5x&7"
				""
				"&8Every chunk you burn now is four you will not have later. Smelt what you need for the next machine and stockpile the rest - a chest of raw chunks is the best investment you can make early."
				""
				"&7Copper is the one people under-collect. Create runs on brass, brass runs on copper, and you will want hundreds.&r"
			]
			icon: "exdeorum:iron_ore_chunk"
			id: "2101000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "2101000000000106"
				item: "minecraft:gravel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Sift gravel for metal"
			tasks: [
				{
					count: 6L
					id: "2101000000000206"
					item: "exdeorum:iron_ore_chunk"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 4L
					id: "2101000000000207"
					item: "exdeorum:copper_ore_chunk"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&aOre From Gravel"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000005"]
			description: [
				"Smelt your iron ore chunks into ingots. The first real metal in the sky - it goes into hammers, meshes, and your first machines."
				""
				"&e&lWhere your early iron goes.&r Budget for these before you spend it on armour:"
				"&7- &fIron Hammer&7 - lasts far longer than stone and is the tool you use most early on."
				"&7- &fIron Mesh&7 - the first mesh that pays for itself. Gets you the rarer chunks."
				"&7- &fBlast Furnace&7 - 5 iron, and the only route to Sky Steel."
				"&7- &fBuckets&7 - you will need several for lava, water and the crucible."
				""
				"&8Armour can wait. You are not fighting anything yet, and every ingot spent on a chestplate is an ingot not spent on the machine that makes more iron."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:iron_ingot"
			id: "2101000000000006"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2101000000000107"
				item: "minecraft:iron_block"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Iron from stone soup"
			tasks: [{
				count: 8L
				id: "2101000000000208"
				item: "minecraft:iron_ingot"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&aFirst Iron"
			x: -6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000006"]
			description: [
				"Breaking cobble by hand got you this far. Now stop."
				""
				"A &eCobble Gen Tier1&r is a block that just... makes cobblestone, into its own buffer. Hopper it out, pipe it away, walk off. It never stops."
				""
				"&7Recipe: 6 logs around a &eGlass&r, with a &eWater Bucket&r and a &eLava Bucket&r either side.&r"
				""
				"&cIt eats both buckets&r - but you can bucket your lava source back up out of your cobble generator first. That is why this waits until you have iron."
				""
				"&eFive tiers&r, each faster than the last: &7logs &8→&r cobble &8→&r iron &8→&r gold &8→&r diamond&r. Upgrade when the buffer can't keep up."
				""
				"&8Feeds straight into hammers, sieves, and eventually your ME system. Cobble is the bottom of every chain in this pack - automate it early."
			]
			icon: "cobblefordays:tier_1"
			id: "0AC0000000000002"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 8
					id: "0AC0000000000103"
					item: "minecraft:glass"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "0AC0000000000104"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 40
				}
			]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Cobble while you sleep"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0AC0000000000202"
				item: "cobblefordays:tier_1"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&aCobble On Tap"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000006"]
			description: [
				"A Blast Furnace smelts metal twice as fast - and it is the only way to reach the heat needed for Sky Steel. Build one."
				""
				"&e&lWhy this matters more than it looks.&r &7Sky Steel&r is the backbone of the early game - it goes into the Sky Assembler, the Crucible line, and the keystone bridges that unlock Mekanism, AE2 and Powah. A normal furnace will never make it. This block is the gate."
				""
				"&7Blast Furnaces only accept ores, raw metals and metal tools - no food, no sand, no wood. Keep an ordinary furnace running alongside it.&r"
				""
				"&8Build two or three. Fuel is cheap once the cobble engine runs, and parallel furnaces beat one fast furnace when you are smelting stacks of chunks."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:blast_furnace"
			id: "210100000000000C"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "2101000000000108"
				item: "minecraft:coal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Hotter than hot"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2101000000000209"
				item: "minecraft:blast_furnace"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&aHotter Than Hot"
			x: -4.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000001"]
			description: [
				"A Crook strips leaves for saplings and silk worms without destroying them. Silk worms breed into string - and string makes your first mesh. It also speeds sapling farming for endless wood."
				""
				"&e&lWhy the crook and not your fist.&r Breaking leaves by hand mostly gives you nothing. The crook multiplies sapling drops and is the &lonly&r way to get silk worms - which matters, because in a void world there are no sheep, no spiders and no other route to string."
				""
				"&7Put a silk worm on a leaf block and it slowly eats it, leaving &fstring&r behind. Set up a wall of leaves and a handful of worms and you have a passive string farm - the first thing in this pack that works while you are not looking at it.&r"
				""
				"&8String makes your first mesh, and the mesh is what starts the entire resource chain. Everything you build for the next hundred hours traces back to a worm on a leaf."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "exdeorum:crook"
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
				}
			}
			id: "210100000000000A"
			rewards: [{
				count: 4
				id: "2101000000000109"
				item: "minecraft:string"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Leaves, saplings, silk worms"
			tasks: [{
				id: "210100000000020A"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "exdeorum:crook"
					tag: {
						Damage: 0
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&aThe Crook"
			x: -14.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000001"]
			description: [
				"An &eEx Deorum Barrel&r is the cheapest thing you will ever build and it solves your water problem."
				""
				"&b&lWater from a tree.&r Drop &eleaves&r or saplings into a barrel and they render down into water - no bucket, no rain, no ice required. A barrel left out in the rain fills on its own too."
				""
				"Barrels also compost plant matter into &edirt&r, which matters more than it sounds: dirt is what you sieve for your first stone, so a barrel is renewable ground as well as renewable water."
			]
			icon: "exdeorum:oak_barrel"
			id: "210100000000000D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "210100000000010A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 20
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Compost, water and lava"
			tasks: [{
				id: "210100000000020D"
