			}]
			title: "&aThe Barrel"
			x: -16.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000004"]
			description: [
				"Your string mesh catches the common drops. A &eFlint Mesh&r catches more."
				""
				"Sieve gravel for flint (or craft flint from gravel), then craft the Flint Mesh. This is upgrade one of five: &7string &8→ &7flint &8→ &7iron &8→ &7diamond &8→ &7netherite&r."
			]
			icon: "exdeorum:flint_mesh"
			id: "2101000000000007"
			rewards: [{
				id: "210100000000010B"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 20
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Mesh upgrade 1 of 5"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2101000000000221"
				item: "exdeorum:flint_mesh"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&aSharper Sieving: Flint"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000007"]
			description: [
				"The &eIron Mesh&r unlocks the metal chunks in real quantity - osmium, tin and lead now appear alongside iron and gold. Craft it once you have iron to spare."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the mesh that changes the pack.&r &7Osmium&r is the reason. It does not appear on string or flint meshes at all, and Mekanism - the whole electric tier - is built on it. Every Steel Casing, every circuit, every machine frame wants osmium."
				""
				"&7You can also bridge to osmium with a SkyForge Industrial Keystone, but sieving is the scalable route. The keystone gets you started; the iron mesh keeps you supplied.&r"
				""
				"&8Once this is running, put a second sieve on flint and keep it there. Flint still out-performs iron for a few common drops, and you will want both flowing at once."
			]
			icon: "exdeorum:iron_mesh"
			id: "2101000000000008"
			rewards: [{
				id: "210100000000010C"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Mesh upgrade 2 of 5"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2101000000000222"
				item: "exdeorum:iron_mesh"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&aIron Mesh"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2101000000000008"]
			description: [
				"Sieve enough gravel and diamonds fall out. Turn them into a &eDiamond Mesh&r - the tier that pulls the pack's rarest sieve drops and lasts almost forever."
				""
				"&e&lWhat the diamond tier is really for.&r It is not about new drops so much as &lrates&r. Everything the iron mesh gave you now comes faster, and the genuinely scarce things - the ones you need in bulk far later - start appearing often enough to plan around."
				""
				"&7Sieve &fdust&r with this, not just gravel. Dust is where redstone, lapis and glowstone live, and those become the bottleneck the moment you start building Mekanism machines in quantity.&r"
				""
				"&8Netherite mesh exists above this one, but the jump is small compared to iron-to-diamond. Do not stall here chasing it - get diamond, automate, and move on to Create."
			]
			icon: "exdeorum:diamond_mesh"
			id: "2101000000000009"
			rewards: [{
				count: 2
				id: "210100000000010D"
				item: "minecraft:diamond"
